commit a5ff01d4883d1dd51efa73e97f65e8cce8acb9dc

C03: screen-reading drafts unescape copied JSON and the code-shape checks run on the masked copy (SCREEN1423)

SCREEN1421 measured «que ves en mi pantalla» (H0458/H0593): capture and read completed and verified, and every draft quoted three recognized lines faithfully, but a screen line ended in «"key": false,» (a terminal window of the root was on screen) and compose_visible_defect vetoed each draft as internal_code. Three causes: the «: true/false» and localTime/stepCount checks ran on the unmasked text; the line masking in observed_response_literals split observed.text on newlines while the provider joins it with spaces (the lines live in observed.layout.lines[].text), so no quoted line was ever masked; and the model copied the JSON escapes of the prompt («\"», «\n») into the quotation, so the quoted line differed from the recognized one anyway.

llm.compose_user_message: screen_clip unescapes copied JSON escapes («\"» → «"», «\» → «\», «\n»/«\r»/«\t» → space) in a draft of a verified screen reading before the checks and before publication.
llm.compose_visible_defect: the «: true/false» and localTime/stepCount code shapes are judged on the masked copy (vocabulary_text), like the snake and dotted shapes.
observed_response_literals.without_observed_names: the recognized layout lines join the masked names.

Offline probe on the SCREEN1421 private audit: the 36 vetoed drafts of cases 1 and 2 pass every veto after the unescape; drafts that leak «readOnly: false», «localTime» or «mission_completed» are still vetoed as internal_code. Mind only, no App recompilation. Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


